# 0002 · Standard recipes that only apply to app repositories

- Status: accepted
- Date: @@TODAY@@
- Guide version: @@GUIDE_VERSION@@
- Rules concerned: DEL-CI-001

## Context

Guide 501 lists standard recipes for every repository. Some of them act on
things only an app has: generated artefacts, a portal or integration API, a
minimal site with one app installed.

## Decision

| Recipe | In this repository |
|---|---|
| `generate` | Runs, and reports that there are no generators |
| `check-generated` | Runs (`git diff --exit-code` after `generate`) and is part of `just ci` |
| `api-diff` | Prints `not applicable` and passes: the platform has no API; each app diffs its own at level 1 |
| `test-backend site=minimal` | Refused: the platform tests the full site only (level 2); apps run the minimal site at level 1 |

## Consequences

- Every standard recipe exists, so tooling and people can call any of them in
  any repository.
- If the platform ever gains generated files or an API, the recipe gets a real
  body and this ADR is superseded.
